@prefix deliberation: <http://example.org/agora/deliberation#> .
@prefix : <http://example.org/agora/deliberation#> .
@prefix ag:   <http://example.org/agora#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<http://example.org/agora/deliberation> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Agora deliberation" ;
    rdfs:comment """The WHETHER, extracted. Whether to look and whether to pursue used to be welded into the bidder — a reading arrived and value_bid's cede was the whole of deciding — which meant the one place this project intends to seat a model had no seam to drop into. It is a family now: given where the agent stands against what it wants (the gap) and what it is already doing (the standing intentions), a deliberator names the next move, and the acting modules carry it out.

**What stays out is everything but the whether.** The HOW is the actor's — a bid's quantity and price are deterministic code, per knowledge/decisions/deterministic-bid.md, whoever said to bid. The KEEPING is intention's: a deliberator may read what stands and never writes the ledger, because deciding and remembering what was decided are different abilities. And a HOST's trigger is not here at all: a host has no gap — its "whether to sell" is the strategic-supplier seam, a stake in the market rather than in a subject.

See knowledge/decisions/an-intention-is-an-amortised-deliberation.md.""" .

#################  The capability  #################
#
#  The family this whole roadmap was run to open. `deliberation:Reflex` is the old welded chain
#  as a member: pursue what sits below the aim, look when you cannot see — deterministic, free,
#  always a valid fallback, and extracted UNCHANGED so the seam provably carries the existing
#  behaviour before anything cleverer steps into it. `deliberation:Consulting` is the reason
#  for the extraction and is deliberately unimplemented.

:DeliberationCapability a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ag:Capability ;
    rdfs:label "Deliberation capability" ;
    rdfs:comment "The family. Anything that turns the gap and the standing commitments into the next move is one of these, so an acting module asks 'should I?' without knowing how the answer is reached — which is what lets the answerer be replaced without touching a line of the actors." .

:Reflex a :DeliberationCapability ; rdfs:label "Reflex" ;
    rdfs:comment "Answers from the gap's sign and nothing else: below the aim, acquire; cannot see, observe; otherwise nothing. The welded chain the bidder used to BE, now a member the bidder asks — extracted unchanged, so every round test that held before holds after. Granted by the same premise as intention:Keeping, because deciding and committing are meaningful under exactly the same conditions: a stake, and a lever to act on it." .

:Planning a :DeliberationCapability ; rdfs:label "Planning" ;
    rdfs:comment "The reflex, one level up: bounded search over menu rows, depth 2 and no deeper, for the agent whose LEVERS COMPOSE — a lever whose effect makes another of its levers meaningful. Its premise is the dealer's: acting for a source it offers, refillable from a source another offers, so acquiring upstream is what makes offering downstream possible. It subsumes the reflex (a planner at depth two contains depth one) and adds exactly one deduced goal past the region: the hosted lot must be serveable — stock at least the lot is what every downstream buyer's Acquire silently preconditions, so the dealer pursues it the way a fern pursues its aim. The plan it holds — acquire, then offer — is a path of menu rows, never surgery the agent imagines onto the world; see knowledge/decisions/a-plan-is-a-path-of-graph-diffs.md. Search stays bounded by construction: if a domain ever wants depth past the dealer's two, that is a different decision, taken then." .

:Consulting a :DeliberationCapability ; rdfs:label "Consulting" ;
    rdfs:comment "The agent asks a model what next, over its beliefs, the T-Box, the gap and what already stands — one call emitting a move from THIS vocabulary's menu, never free text-to-action. RESERVED: declared because seating a model is the reason the family exists and the T-Box should say so; unimplemented because the seam had to demonstrably carry Reflex first. What it will NOT be allowed to do is already fixed: the bid number stays deterministic (the model picks whether and when, code computes how much), an intention it proposes validates against the same shapes or is not adopted, and the keeper's patience bounds how often it is consulted at all — which is what makes it affordable. See knowledge/decisions/llm-heavy-deliberation.md, as amended." .
